Package: sbert
Type: Package
Title: Sentence Embeddings with 'Sentence-BERT' Models
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Mohammed",
    family = "Saqr",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "mohammed.saqr@uef.fi",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5881-3109")
  )
Description: Computes sentence embeddings in R without requiring
    'Python' by running revision-pinned 'Sentence-BERT' models through
    'ONNX Runtime'. Implements model-specific tokenization,
    attention-mask-aware mean pooling, L2 normalization, cosine
    similarity, deterministic semantic topic clustering, and class-based
    term weighting following Reimers and Gurevych (2019)
    <doi:10.18653/v1/D19-1410>. Topic models are evaluated with intrinsic
    coherence (UMass and normalized pointwise mutual information) and
    diversity metrics, and summarized with deterministic base-graphics
    visualizations. Model files are downloaded only after an explicit user
    request and are stored outside the package library.
